    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d479-a1">

                <pb facs="0832" n="738" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg738"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    167.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mariscal to Mr. Manning</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-06-25"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 25,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: Referring to your excellency’s
                    note of date May 19 last, concerning a complaint by Messrs. Pomares &amp;
                    Cushman, of New York, a copy of which your excellency was pleased to forward to
                    me, I have the honor to inclose copy of the reply sent me by the secretary of
                    the treasury giving the decision of the Mexican Government upon the matter.</p>
                <p>In his reply the secretary of the treasury calls attention to the fact that
                    Messrs. Pomares &amp; Cushman showed at least bad taste in the selection of
                    instances upon which to predicate their criticisms touching the fiscal
                    procedures and acts of the customs employe’s in Mexico. In the case of the two
                    shipments they specify, the fine in one was even less than they supposed, and
                    its imposition was discountenanced and reproved by the treasury department, and
                    ere this probably repaid to the complainants; while in the other case the heavy
                    damages lamented were limited to $1.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Igno. Mariscal.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
